==Battleground==
*1 [[King Wahwah]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Daboo of the Dead]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*10 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage features two powerful Omni Strike pushers and some really nasty peons. You'll likely rely on spamming [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] as much as possible to whittle down Daboo's HP at range while dealing with the Reds AND stop Wahwah from pushing too much.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]: A disposable melee attacker that can easily exploit Daboo's long attack delay to sneak in a few hits and deal devastating damage, although you'd have to keep up with your Anti-Reds for a chance at this.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier's disposability, [[Massive Damage]] to Red enemies and decent stats makes it an excellent choice for whittling down groups of nasty Reds as long as you can keep them out of its small blindspot.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]: Manic Island is a powerful anti-Red melee attacker that's cheap and effective with its [[Strong Against]] ability. It can hold the line for a bit while your other units rain down carnage.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]]: Slime's high damage, good cooldown time and level 5 [[Wave Attack]] makes it the excellent choice for chipping both Wahwah and Daboo. Because Ginger Snache frequently spawns, it gets lots of opportunities with a bit of timing.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Bullet Train's high damage, while inferior to your specialists, still shouldn't be ignored, as Bullet Train can easily get a hit in on Wahwah when he is exposed and his [[Knockback]] effect can reset Bullet Train's attack animation. It's also useful for just dealing damage in general.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: A Can Can [[Talents|Talented]] with Move Speed Up and [[Money Up]] is very similar to Bullet Train in that they are both great for putting out damage to wipe the frontline clean, and Can Can's [[Slow]] ability makes Shy Boys a bit easier to deal with, despite also being Single Attack.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Stone's extreme health, [[Immune to Knockback|Immunity to Knockback]] and [[Immune to Slow|Slow]] as well as high speed makes it an excellent supplementary meatshield to bait Wahwah into attacking and to stall the peons when they're putting up too much pressure.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Greater Balrog's [[Strengthen]], Defense, Cost and Attack Talents are all great for making him useful in the stage. His devastating damage can easily wipe Shy Boys from the field and deal great damage to Daboo if used well while his low cooldown means you can send him rather frequently.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: Lasvoss' True Form is difficult to acquire, and expensive and may not get in the all-important hit. However, his Strengthen, [[Savage Blow]]s, Immunity to Knockback and Slow can easily allow him to exploit his very high damage regardless of how unreliable they may get. His cooldown is lower than the average Uber, and you'll often find yourself being able to deploy him a few times throughout this endurance stage.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: With a combination of high health, high damage, and Immunity to Knockback, Kai can be a very resilient fighter as it ignores King Wahwah's Knockback and can tank both Daboo's and Wahwah's attacks. She can help clear out the Ginger Snaches with good peon-clearers such as Slime Cat so that Kai does not waste an attack.

